/* ===================== CLINICAL LABS: L1 blood gas interpretation · L2 lab patterns =====================
   Blood gases are generated to be internally consistent: pH = 6.1 + log10(HCO₃⁻ ÷ (0.03 × PaCO₂)).
   Compensation rules used (state them in the question when a number depends on them):
     metabolic acidosis  PaCO₂ = 1.5 × HCO₃⁻ + 8 (± 2)          metabolic alkalosis  PaCO₂ = 40 + 0.7 × (HCO₃⁻ − 24) (± 2)
     respiratory acidosis HCO₃⁻ ↑ 1 (acute) or 3.5 (chronic) per 10 mmHg PaCO₂ above 40
     respiratory alkalosis HCO₃⁻ ↓ 2 (acute) or 4 (chronic) per 10 mmHg PaCO₂ below 40
   Needs gdata.js, study.js. */
